; 40-format.kurt

; `format` chooses how formulas are printed in the log: `normal` (the
; default, close to how you typed it) or `sexpr` (fully-parenthesised
; s-expressions, useful for seeing the exact tree structure Kurt parsed).
; (For a LaTeX document of a proof, see `scripts/kurt2latex.py`.)

bool A, B, C

format sexpr
use A
use B
A and B                 ; printed as `(and A B)`

format normal
use C
A and C                  ; back to the default look: `A and C`

; `format` with no argument reports the current setting:
format
